# Kubri Media — Project Rules

## Positioning

Kubri Media is a boutique B2B creator broker. Name = Arabic for "bridge."
Tagline: "Kubri. Your bridge to technical audiences."
Voice: structural, reliable, infrastructure — NOT flashy marketing agency.
Audience: B2B SaaS / DevTool founders and technical marketers.

## Vocabulary

- SAY: "technical creators", "developer creators", "technical channels", "tutorial", "video"
- DON'T SAY: "YouTubers", "influencers", "content creators", "viral", "drama", "hack"
- Never use emoji in the UI. Never use exclamation marks.

## Design tokens

- Background: slate-950. Cards: slate-900/50 with white/10 border.
- Text: slate-100 primary, slate-400 secondary, slate-500 tertiary.
- Accent (ONLY accent): indigo. Buttons indigo-500 → hover indigo-400.
  Highlights/eyebrows: indigo-400 or indigo-300.
- Typography: Inter. tracking-tight on headings. Uppercase mono-style
  eyebrows with letter-spacing (text-xs, tracking-[0.2em], text-indigo-400).
- Corners: rounded-2xl cards, rounded-lg buttons. Never 0-radius.
- Spacing: sections py-24 md:py-32. Content max-w-6xl, side px-6.
- Motion: 150–300ms color/opacity transitions only. No bounce, no spring,
  no scroll animations unless explicitly requested.
- Focus: focus-visible:ring-2 ring-indigo-400/50 on every interactive element.

## Do not

- No stock photos, no people, no illustrations of humans.
- No gradients as decorative overlays on text or cards.
- Single soft ambient glow behind the hero is allowed — that's the only gradient.
- No new dependencies without asking.
- No new routes/pages. Single landing page.
- Do not touch copy in docs/COPY.md without explicit instruction.

## Structure

app/layout.tsx, app/page.tsx, app/globals.css
components/Navbar.tsx, Hero.tsx, Problem.tsx, Solution.tsx, Pricing.tsx,
Guardrails.tsx, Footer.tsx
